        32.93328857421875
      ],
      "text": "Second",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-LightCn",
      "size": 9.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        63.09400177001953,
        21.884788513183594,
        86.86299896240234,
        32.93328857421875
      ],
      "text": "edition",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-LightCn",
      "size": 9.5,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        82.18360900878906,
        321.8758850097656,
        99.03961181640625
      ],
      "text": "1.4\t H  TB",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Black-SC70",
      "size": 14.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        131.3571014404297,
        86.19041442871094,
        510.19610595703125,
        97.98960876464844
      ],
      "text": "ow does management of in children and adolescents",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Black-SC70",
      "size": 9.800000190734863,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        281.3124084472656,
        100.58363342285156,
        289.0964050292969,
        117.43963623046875
      ],
      "text": "?",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Black-SC70",
      "size": 14.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        121.03939819335938,
        104.59043884277344,
        281.0823974609375,
        116.38963317871094
      ],
      "text": "differ from that in adults",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Black-SC70",
      "size": 9.800000190734863,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        125.13238525390625,
        513.4144897460938,
        138.48388671875
      ],
      "text": "Children can present with TB disease at any age but most commonly, in TB-endemic",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        141.12890625,
        513.3799438476562,
        154.48040771484375
      ],
      "text": "countries, between 1 and 4 years. Pulmonary TB is the commonest type of TB in children.",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        157.12542724609375,
        513.4260864257812,
        170.4769287109375
      ],
      "text": "Extrapulmonary disease is also common (around 30-40% of cases) and can present in a",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        173.1219482421875,
        513.4261474609375,
        186.47344970703125
      ],
      "text": "wide variety of anatomical sites. Children who develop TB disease usually do so within",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        189.04946899414062,
        513.471923828125,
        202.469970703125
      ],
      "text": "(1) 1 year following infection  , which is why the presentation of TB in children is an",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-LightItali",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        205.04598999023438,
        487.6200256347656,
        218.46649169921875
      ],
      "text": "M. tuberculosis indicator of recent and ongoing transmission of   in the community.",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-LightItali",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        229.62152099609375,
        513.368408203125,
        242.9730224609375
      ],
      "text": "Infants and young children (especially those under 2 years) are at greatest risk of",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        245.6180419921875,
        513.4259033203125,
        258.96954345703125
      ],
      "text": "developing severe, disseminated disease associated with a high morbidity and mortality.",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        261.61456298828125,
        513.4144897460938,
        274.966064453125
      ],
      "text": "In infants, the time between infection and disease can be shorter than in older children,",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        277.611083984375,
        287.81884765625,
        290.96258544921875
      ],
      "text": "and the presentation may be more acute.",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        302.11761474609375,
        513.3915405273438,
        315.4691162109375
      ],
      "text": "Adolescence is associated with an increased risk of the development of TB, which",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        318.1141357421875,
        513.3914794921875,
        331.46563720703125
      ],
      "text": "usually presents as adult-type pulmonary disease and is often sputum smear-positive. TB",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        334.1106262207031,
        440.53900146484375,
        347.4621276855469
      ],
      "text": "in adolescence is thus frequently infectious and a source of transmission.",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        358.61712646484375,
        513.4719848632812,
        371.9686279296875
      ],
      "text": "After contact with an infectious source case, most immunocompetent children present",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        374.6136169433594,
        513.4720458984375,
        387.9651184082031
      ],
      "text": "with nonspecific symptoms of a chronic disease. The presentation in infants may be",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        390.610107421875,
        513.3800659179688,
        403.96160888671875
      ],
      "text": "more acute, resembling acute severe, recurrent or persistent pneumonia. TB should",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        406.6065979003906,
        513.4146728515625,
        419.9580993652344
      ],
      "text": "be suspected when there is a poor response to appropriate conventional antibiotics. In",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        422.60308837890625,
        513.4949951171875,
        435.95458984375
      ],
      "text": "such situations, there is often an identifiable source case, usually the mother or primary",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        438.5995788574219,
        131.03941345214844,
        451.9510803222656
      ],
      "text": "caregiver.",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        463.1060791015625,
        513.3799438476562,
        476.45758056640625
      ],
      "text": "Children with TB, especially older children and adolescents, can be infectious although",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        479.1025695800781,
        513.4146728515625,
        492.4540710449219
      ],
      "text": "most are not. Rather than being a major infection concern, TB in children is an indicator",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        495.09906005859375,
        444.6098937988281,
        508.4505615234375
      ],
      "text": "of recent and ongoing transmission of M. tuberculosis in the community.",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        519.6055297851562,
        513.3798828125,
        532.95703125
      ],
      "text": "Generally speaking, adolescents – a particular at-risk group – are not specifically",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        535.60205078125,
        513.4030151367188,
        548.9535522460938
      ],
      "text": "highlighted in treatment guidelines for TB and deserve greater attention in this context. It",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        551.5985717773438,
        513.4951171875,
        564.9500732421875
      ],
      "text": "is recognized that TB and TB/HIV in adolescents and adults are largely similar, for example",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        567.5950317382812,
        513.4029541015625,
        580.946533203125
      ],
      "text": "in clinical presentation, anti-TB drug dosages and disease management. However,",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        583.591552734375,
        513.3685302734375,
        596.9430541992188
      ],
      "text": "adolescents form a particularly vulnerable group that is not at risk only for disease:",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        599.5880737304688,
        513.3799438476562,
        612.9395751953125
      ],
      "text": "there are often important psychosocial challenges, unique challenges for autonomy and",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        615.5845336914062,
        513.41455078125,
        628.93603515625
      ],
      "text": "adherence, and the usual challenges of satisfactory transition from paediatric to adult",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        631.5810546875,
        513.4835815429688,
        644.9325561523438
      ],
      "text": "health service provision. Adolescents with TB often develop an adult-like disease and",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        647.5775756835938,
        221.77438354492188,
        660.9290771484375
      ],
      "text": "thus may well be infectious.",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        683.0150756835938,
        129.58740234375,
        699.87109375
      ],
      "text": "1.5\t E",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Black-SC70",
      "size": 14.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        129.8032989501953,
        687.0219116210938,
        206.29275512695312,
        698.8211059570312
      ],
      "text": "thical issues",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Black-SC70",
      "size": 9.800000190734863,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        707.5639038085938,
        513.3914794921875,
        720.9154052734375
      ],
      "text": "Children are a particularly vulnerable population and their rights must be respected.",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        723.5604248046875,
        513.4721069335938,
        736.9119262695312
      ],
      "text": "The key ethical issues that must be considered in implementing TB control strategies",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        739.556884765625,
        513.4028930664062,
        752.9083862304688
      ],
      "text": "or research are as important and relevant for children as for any other age group.",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        755.5534057617188,
        513.3915405273438,
        768.9049072265625
      ],
      "text": "Governments are obliged to provide universal access to high-quality TB diagnosis and",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        771.5499267578125,
        513.4605102539062,
        784.9014282226562
      ],
      "text": "treatment and to address the social determinants that are largely responsible for the",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        14.202799797058105,
        805.8439331054688,
        36.44280242919922,
        835.8439331054688
      ],
      "text": "12",
      "font": "HelveticaNeue-Light",
      "size": 20.0,
      "type": "heading_main"
    }
  ]
}